# PDF Import Improvements — Implementation Plan

Improve the PDF import system with better error handling, scanned PDF support via OCR.space API, batch processing UI, large PDF chunking, and AI parsing optimization.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **OCR.space API Key Required**: You'll need a free API key from [ocr.space/ocrapi](https://ocr.space/ocrapi). Free tier: 500 requests/day, 1MB max file size, 3 pages max per PDF. This is sufficient for most Ayurvedic distributor price lists. If you need larger capacity, paid plans start at $30/month.

> [!WARNING]
> **Two Import Modals Exist**: The codebase has two separate import UIs — [ImportMedicinesModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/ImportMedicinesModal.tsx) and [import-price-list.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/medicine/import-price-list.tsx). Both will be updated with the same improvements for consistency.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Structured Error Handling in Backend

#### [MODIFY] [aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts)

- Add a new `ParseResult` type that returns `{ medicines: ParsedMedicine[], pdfType: 'searchable' | 'scanned' | 'unknown', error?: string, errorCode?: string }`
- Add OCR.space integration: when pdf2json returns no text, call OCR.space API to extract text from scanned PDFs
- The fallback flow: `pdf2json → OCR.space → AI parse`
- Add `detectPdfType()` helper that checks if extracted text is empty/minimal
- Export [parsePDFWithAI()](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#334-436) to return `ParseResult` instead of raw array

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/api/medicines/import/route.ts)

- Return structured error responses with `errorCode` field (e.g., `SCANNED_PDF_NO_OCR_KEY`, `SCANNED_PDF_TOO_LARGE`, `NO_TEXT_FOUND`, `PARSE_FAILED`, `OCR_FAILED`)
- Return `pdfType` in success response for UI display

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/api/medicine/import-price-list/route.ts)

- This file contains its own inline parser. Add the same OCR.space fallback and structured errors here.

---

### Component 2: OCR.space Integration

#### [MODIFY] [aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts)

New function `ocrWithOcrSpace(pdfBuffer: Buffer)`:
- Sends PDF as base64 to `https://api.ocr.space/parse/image`
- Uses `OCR_SPACE_API_KEY` from env
- Handles multi-page PDFs (up to 3 pages on free tier)
- Returns extracted text string
- Graceful error handling: returns empty string on failure

#### [MODIFY] [.env.example](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/.env.example)

- Add `OCR_SPACE_API_KEY=""` with comment

---

### Component 3: Smart UI Error Messages

#### [MODIFY] [ImportMedicinesModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/ImportMedicinesModal.tsx)

- Add smart error banner with icons and guidance based on `errorCode`:
  - `SCANNED_PDF_NO_OCR_KEY` → "This is a scanned PDF. OCR is not configured. Contact admin."
  - `SCANNED_PDF_TOO_LARGE` → "Scanned PDF too large for OCR. Try a smaller file or searchable PDF."
  - `NO_TEXT_FOUND` → "Could not extract any text. Ensure the PDF contains medicine data."
  - `OCR_FAILED` → "OCR processing failed. Try again or use a searchable PDF."
  - Generic fallback for unknown errors
- Add a PDF type indicator after successful parse ("✅ Searchable PDF" or "🔍 Scanned PDF — processed via OCR")
- Show processing phase: "Extracting text..." → "Running OCR..." → "AI parsing..."

#### [MODIFY] [import-price-list.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/medicine/import-price-list.tsx)

- Same error handling improvements as ImportMedicinesModal

